Itanium C++ ABI 2.4 II.3 layout with a virtual base that itself has a
virtual base (`V : virtual W', `B1 : virtual V', `B2 : virtual X',
`D : B1, B2'): the virtual bases follow the non-virtual part in inheritance
graph order (V, W, X), each with its own virtual pointer where it is a
dynamic class; sizes and offsets are those of g++ 13 and clang 18 on
x86-64 (D = 56 bytes).
